00:06:56.160 --> 00:06:59.540
Going on from Cloud
Functions to App Engine--

00:06:59.540 --> 00:07:01.130
so as I mentioned
before, App Engine

00:07:01.130 --> 00:07:04.160
is our 10-year-old
serverless offering.

00:07:04.160 --> 00:07:06.620
It was one of the earliest
serverless offerings.

00:07:06.620 --> 00:07:08.360
If you want to build
your traditional web

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:10.940
app on your favorite language
such as Node.js, Python,

00:07:10.940 --> 00:07:14.030
or Java, you can
use App Engine along

00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:17.787
with frameworks such as
Express, Flask, and Spring.

00:07:17.787 --> 00:07:20.120
The product [INAUDIBLE] use
advanced management features

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:22.910
such as application
versioning, traffic splitting,

00:07:22.910 --> 00:07:25.310
IP firewalls, logging,
monitoring, and so on.

00:07:28.390 --> 00:07:33.490
We've [INAUDIBLE],, which are all
GA, such as PHP, GO, Node.js.

00:07:33.490 --> 00:07:36.820
Further, we're really excited to
have Java 11 on App Engine, as

00:07:36.820 --> 00:07:37.420
well as Ruby.

00:07:41.900 --> 00:07:43.928
Further on moving
down, I want to talk

00:07:43.928 --> 00:07:45.470
about the most recent
offering, which

00:07:45.470 --> 00:07:48.710
is Cloud Run, which
is serverless agility

00:07:48.710 --> 00:07:50.630
for containerized apps.

00:07:50.630 --> 00:07:53.000
We've talked about it
a lot in Next recently,

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:57.500
and I want to elaborate a
little bit more about it.

00:07:57.500 --> 00:07:59.680
What this basically means
is taking a container

00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:03.100
from production to
deployment in seconds.

00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:06.610
Just give us a container in
any language or any library,

00:08:06.610 --> 00:08:09.170
and with a single command,
it gets immediately deployed

00:08:09.170 --> 00:08:13.220
in Google Cloud and you
have a URL in seconds.

00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:16.955
Further, we consider this to be
a natively serverless offering.

00:08:16.955 --> 00:08:19.580
What this basically means is you
don't-- as I mentioned before,

00:08:19.580 --> 00:08:21.200
you don't have to
manage any servers.

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:23.210
Just focus on writing your code.

00:08:23.210 --> 00:08:24.620
It scales up very quickly.

00:08:24.620 --> 00:08:26.090
It scales down to zero.

00:08:26.090 --> 00:08:28.100
And you pay exactly
for what you use,

00:08:28.100 --> 00:08:31.370
the lifecycle of a request.

00:08:31.370 --> 00:08:33.860
And it's one experience
where you want to want it.

00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:37.330
What this basically means is
you have a unified developer

00:08:37.330 --> 00:08:40.890
experience on where you want
to run your application.

00:08:40.890 --> 00:08:42.380
For example, if
you want to run it

00:08:42.380 --> 00:08:45.530
on a fully managed deployment
within Google Cloud, you could.

00:08:45.530 --> 00:08:47.870
If you want to run
it on GKE, Cloud Run

00:08:47.870 --> 00:08:50.000
works on Cloud
Run and GKE, where

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:52.460
you get additional
control on your cluster.

00:08:52.460 --> 00:08:55.100
And if you don't run it
on Google Cloud at all,

00:08:55.100 --> 00:08:58.140
this entire technology is based
on what is called Knative.

00:08:58.140 --> 00:09:01.520
And you can run Knative on your
on-prem systems on Kubernetes

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:03.272
and run your containers there.

00:09:03.272 --> 00:09:04.730
By doing this, we
want to make sure

00:09:04.730 --> 00:09:07.460
that you have the full spectrum
of offerings across the Cloud

00:09:07.460 --> 00:09:10.180
and on-prem systems with
zero vendor lock-in.

00:09:13.710 --> 00:09:15.720
So now, what's the Java
story for serverless?

00:09:18.540 --> 00:09:20.540
So we're excited to
announce, as I mentioned,

00:09:20.540 --> 00:09:24.020
Java 8 on Google
Cloud Functions.

00:09:24.020 --> 00:09:28.680
Furthermore, we have Java
11 on App Engine standard.

00:09:28.680 --> 00:09:29.940
It's a great offering.

00:09:29.940 --> 00:09:33.282
And I highly recommend
you to try it.

00:09:33.282 --> 00:09:34.990
And then we have Java
on Cloud Run, where

00:09:34.990 --> 00:09:37.390
you can run your favorite
framework, such as Spring

00:09:37.390 --> 00:09:41.490
and so on, on our
Cloud Run offering.

00:09:41.490 --> 00:09:43.723
