GUILLAUME LAFORGE: Thank you.

00:09:50.960 --> 00:09:55.310
So Cloud Functions,
App Engine, Cloud

00:09:55.310 --> 00:09:58.480
Run-- we'll demonstrate
the three products.

00:09:58.480 --> 00:10:04.140
So here is the typical screen
from the Cloud Console.

00:10:04.140 --> 00:10:06.370
And we have a
couple of functions,

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:07.755
which are already deployed.

00:10:10.560 --> 00:10:12.525
So when you create a
function, what happens?

00:10:15.090 --> 00:10:17.510
So let's say I have--

00:10:17.510 --> 00:10:19.740
next.

00:10:19.740 --> 00:10:22.890
What's new for you
today, Java developers?

00:10:22.890 --> 00:10:26.860
It's the fact that we now
have this line, Java 8,

00:10:26.860 --> 00:10:28.680
Alpha, that you can see here.

00:10:28.680 --> 00:10:33.190
And it allows me to
write my Java code here.

00:10:33.190 --> 00:10:35.490
So I have a Java file here.

00:10:35.490 --> 00:10:39.570
And I also have a POM.xml
file, because when

00:10:39.570 --> 00:10:43.500
you do a source deployment
of your Java functions,

00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:46.200
we're using Maven to
build your Java code.

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:51.760
But you can also do a fat
