00:13:48.120 --> 00:13:53.490
Testing-- and it should
print hello, Groovy world,

00:13:53.490 --> 00:13:55.040
in a few milliseconds.

00:13:55.040 --> 00:13:56.820
Yes, hello, Groovy world.

00:13:56.820 --> 00:13:58.830
So we saw HTTP functions.

00:13:58.830 --> 00:14:01.620
But we also support
background functions

00:14:01.620 --> 00:14:06.030
such as new file uploaded
to Cloud Storage,

00:14:06.030 --> 00:14:08.130
and you want to be
notified and have

00:14:08.130 --> 00:14:13.930
your functions being invoked
when a new file is stored.

00:14:13.930 --> 00:14:15.720
Pub/Sub-- when you
receive messages

00:14:15.720 --> 00:14:17.940
on a topic from
Pub/Sub, et cetera.

00:14:17.940 --> 00:14:22.280
And actually, I didn't mention
that as I was using the default

00:14:22.280 --> 00:14:26.880
HTTP Select box here.

00:14:26.880 --> 00:14:30.090
But you can also specify, OK, I
want to create a Pub/Sub method

00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:33.060
and you can see-- oh,
this is still Node, sorry.

00:14:33.060 --> 00:14:37.950
And you have some of the samples
here to help you get started.

