00:15:44.280 --> 00:15:49.330
And I wanted to show you
this architecture diagram.

00:15:49.330 --> 00:15:50.800
So what do we have?

00:15:50.800 --> 00:15:53.490
That's an Angular application,
which is also using

00:15:53.490 --> 00:15:57.780
Firebase with an AJAX call.

00:15:57.780 --> 00:16:00.690
It's going to call a
first Java function,

00:16:00.690 --> 00:16:02.970
this HTTP function here.

00:16:02.970 --> 00:16:08.400
We pass the name of the
file, the picture file name,

00:16:08.400 --> 00:16:11.220
as well as the message.

00:16:11.220 --> 00:16:15.390
This function is going to post
a little request on Pub/Sub

00:16:15.390 --> 00:16:17.010
on a particular topic.

00:16:17.010 --> 00:16:23.310
And then this message, because
those four functions here

00:16:23.310 --> 00:16:25.290
in Go, Python,
Node, and Java are

00:16:25.290 --> 00:16:28.740
going to be woken up because
there's a new message coming up

00:16:28.740 --> 00:16:29.650
on a topic.

00:16:29.650 --> 00:16:34.380
So those functions here
are Pub/Sub functions,

00:16:34.380 --> 00:16:36.000
triggered functions.

00:16:36.000 --> 00:16:40.706
Then those functions
will process the picture,

00:16:40.706 --> 00:16:45.990
