00:24:23.240 --> 00:24:25.940
So I mentioned that
we don't have to use

00:24:25.940 --> 00:24:30.170
servlet-based frameworks.

00:24:30.170 --> 00:24:34.050
Here, I'm using actually just
a fat JAR that I compiled here.

00:24:34.050 --> 00:24:35.470
So I'm using Gretel
for the build,

00:24:35.470 --> 00:24:37.820
but it's irrelevant here.

00:24:37.820 --> 00:24:41.240
I created a fat JAR of my
application that I can deploy.

00:24:41.240 --> 00:24:46.430
And notice that I actually
have full control of the entry

00:24:46.430 --> 00:24:53.990
point, meaning that I can pass
things like garbage collection

00:24:53.990 --> 00:24:54.890
